<figure class="flex flex-col gap-4 border-2 border-ink p-4 sm:p-6">
  <p class="font-bold">Same gap in the launch frame does not mean an unstretched string.</p>
  <svg
    viewBox="0 0 300 228"
    class="mx-auto w-full max-w-sm"
    role="img"
    aria-labelledby="bell-fig-title bell-fig-desc"
  >
    <title id="bell-fig-title">Two equally accelerating ships with a string stretched between them</title>
    <desc id="bell-fig-desc">
      Before and after accelerating in the launch frame, the ships have the same separation. The
      gap exceeds the length that a freely moving, unstretched string would occupy at their new
      speed.
    </desc>
    <g fill="currentColor" font-size="17" font-weight="bold">
      <text x="14" y="22">
        Before acceleration
      </text>
      <text x="14" y="146">
        After acceleration
      </text>
    </g>
    <g stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
      <rect x="14" y="64" width="36" height="22" fill="#387a91" />
      <rect x="214" y="64" width="36" height="22" fill="#387a91" />
      <path d="M50 75 H214" stroke="#d7a13d" stroke-width="5" />
      <rect x="14" y="170" width="36" height="22" fill="#387a91" />
      <rect x="214" y="170" width="36" height="22" fill="#387a91" />
      <path d="M50 181 H214" stroke="#bd4b37" stroke-width="5" />
    </g>
    <g fill="currentColor" font-size="16" text-anchor="middle">
      <text x="132" y="110">
        fixed distance in launch frame
      </text>
      <text x="132" y="216">
        moving string is stretched
      </text>
    </g>
    <g fill="currentColor" font-size="20">
      <text x="256" y="82">
        →
      </text>
      <text x="256" y="188">
        →→
      </text>
    </g>
  </svg>
  <figcaption class="text-base leading-normal">
    Both ships gain speed in exactly the same way, so their separation stays fixed as measured
    at launch. Yet an unstretched string moving at their new speed would occupy a shorter length
    in that frame. It is stretched and may break. The arrows and positions are schematic.
  </figcaption>
</figure>
